    229  f318
    230  f318							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    231  f318
    232  f318							; ==============================================================================
    233  f318							; Raft (enemy type 7) — the moving, rideable platform. plans/raft_moving_plan.md
    234  f318							; ==============================================================================
    235  f318							; Entrance: bank0 UEDispatch -> CallPad_RaftBody (sta $1FF5 / jmp $F822) -> here;
    236  f318							; exit: jmp ReturnPad ($FBF8, bank1's twin) -> bank0's jmp UE_Next.
    237  f318							; CallPad rules honoured: no nested CallPad, no bank0 jsr, ZP is shared RAM.
    238  f318							; ZP ALIAS WARNING: this code uses bank0's Temp at $88 (free here — every other
    239  f318							; overscan Temp consumer, the joystick read and the hot-bump flag, ran before
    240  f318							; UpdateEnemies). It must NEVER touch bank1's Temp symbol ($AD = bank0's
    241  f318							; TickCounter — writing that would stall the game timer).
    242  f318							;
    243  f318							; User spec 2026-10-18: floats only on water; carries the player across and
    244  f318							; returns; ~1.5x the player's 1 px/frame; inertia when it starts.
    245  f318							;   Y	     = the water surface, NOT the authored y and NOT a constant: the
    246  f318							;	       surface line drifts 0-3 lines with the TIDE (VBL stages 36+off
    247  f318							;	       into CollisionX, kernel draws the strip as the band's last
    248  f318							;	       (12-off) lines), so the raft is placed at 125+off and its bottom
    249  f318							;	       row sits exactly on the moving surface — it rides the wave the
    250  f318							;	       water does. The rider's pin (top-22 = 103+off, worst case 106)
    251  f318							;	       stays clear of the 125 water-kill line at every tide phase.
    252  f318							;	       This write lands after RefreshEnemyY, so the VBL draws it.
    253  f318							;   Speed   = 1 px on even frames, 2 px on odd (EnemyRamP parity) = 1.5 px/frame.
    254  f318							;   Inertia = a real spin-up ramp: 1 px/frame for ~30 frames (~0.5 s) then the
    255  f318							;	       full 1/2 parity (1.5 avg), so the take-off is heavy. The state
    256  f318							;	       lives in PlayerBombs' ($F0) spare high bits (b7 = ridden flag,
    257  f318							;	       b6-b3 = level) — the ZP map has no free byte and the bomb count
    258  f318							;	       keeps b2-0 (see the kernel EQU contract). Stepping off clears the
    259  f318							;	       flag+level, so the empty raft runs at full speed and the next
    260  f318							;	       take-off ramps again. It also holds the frame it turns around on.
    261  f318							;   Range   = derived from the playfield, no data and no ZP: the model row-2
    262  f318							;	       cell just beyond the raft's leading edge is read from the PF row-2
    263  f318							;	       buffers and a SOLID cell turns it around, so the raft patrols
    264  f318							;	       exactly the open water span of the room.
    265  f318							;   Ride    = the raft is a FERRY: it moves ONLY while the player's box overlaps
    266  f318							;	       its upper rows; step off and it parks immediately (the ramp state
    267  f318							;	       is cleared too, so the next take-off ramps again). While over it a
    268  f318							;	       non-rising player (vyHi >= 0) is pinned to the raft's top with vy
    269  f318							;	       zeroed (gravity must never accumulate into the water) and carried
    270  f318							;	       by the raft's step; thrust up skips the pin but keeps the carry, so
    271  f318							;	       flying off is always possible. Leaving and re-entering the ROOM
    272  f318							;	       resets the raft to its authored spawn x (LoadEnemyRam re-copies
    273  f318							;	       it), which is the "reset" the user asked for.
    274  f318							; In: X = enemy slot. Clobbers A/Y and bank0 Temp ($88).
    275  f318							; ==============================================================================
    276  f318							; RaftCellSolid — is the model row-2 (water row) playfield cell in display
    277  f318							; column A solid? Reflect mapping: CTRLPF $35 (reflect) is the cave default and
    278  f318							; a raft room has no door/bar band to switch it off. IN: A = display col 0..39.
    279  f318							; OUT: Z=1 open (water) / Z=0 solid. Clobbers A/Y.
    280  f318							;   cols 0-3	-> PF0 row 3 ($C6), bit 4+col (PF0 bit 4 = leftmost pixel)
    281  f318							;   cols 4-11	-> PF1 row 3 ($CA), bit 7-(col-4)
    282  f318							;   cols 12-19 -> PF2 row 3 ($CE), bit col-12
    283  f318							; (row 3 = the bottom/water band of a 4-band room. These read $C5/$C8/$CB, the
    284  f318							; rows of the old 3-band stride-3 layout, until 2026-10-28: the raft then turned
    285  f318							; at ceiling/ledge cells that were not on its water row.)
    286  f318							;   cols 20-39 -> the mirrored half: source = 39-col
    287  f318				   RaftCellSolid
    288  f318		       c9 14		      cmp	#20
    289  f31a		       90 05		      bcc	.RCSrc
    290  f31c		       49 ff		      eor	#$ff
    291  f31e		       18		      clc
    292  f31f		       69 28		      adc	#40
    293  f321				   .RCSrc
    294  f321		       a8		      tay
    295  f322		       b9 3a f3 	      lda	RaftCellMasks,Y
    296  f325		       c0 04		      cpy	#4
    297  f327		       b0 03		      bcs	.RCPF1
    298  f329		       25 c6		      and	$C6	; PF0Buf+3: the water row (4 bands; was +2 = band 3)
    299  f32b		       60		      rts
    300  f32c				   .RCPF1
    301  f32c		       c0 0c		      cpy	#12
    302  f32e		       b0 03		      bcs	.RCPF2
    303  f330		       25 ca		      and	$CA	; PF1Buf+3 (stride 4; $C8 was row 1)
    304  f332		       60		      rts
    305  f333				   .RCPF2
    306  f333		       25 ce		      and	$CE	; PF2Buf+3 (stride 4; $CB was row 0)
    307  f335		       60		      rts
    308  f336
    309  f336				   RaftBitTab		; 1 << slot (EnemyBitTable is bank0's ROM, so a
    310  f336		       01 02 04 08	      .byte.b	$01, $02, $04, $08	; 4-byte copy keeps this body bank-local)
    311  f33a
    312  f33a				   RaftCellMasks		; mask for source column 0..19: PF0 cols 0-3 —
    313  f33a		       10 20 40 80	      .byte.b	$10, $20, $40, $80	; PF0 cols 0-3 (bit 4 = leftmost), then
