    485  f97f							; BombMarkWalls (S5.2, moved from bank0) — pinned at $FB10.
    486  f97f							;   On the bomb 1->2 edge: punch the THIN walls in the blast window and
    487  f97f							;   report how many were newly broken (A, caller scores +75 each).
    488  f97f							;   Bomb left-half col +-2, clamped 0..19. Score is NOT done here — pads
    489  f97f							;   cannot nest (ReturnPad switches to bank0), so the bank0 caller adds
    490  f97f							;   +75 per wall.
    491  f97f							;   Plan 5.1b (2026-10-20): the punch is CELL-based — no rect cache. The
    492  f97f							;   PF buffers ARE the map (export: convert_room.pf_values; holes included),
    493  f97f							;   so a bombable wall is found the same way find_rectangles finds a w==2
    494  f97f							;   rect: a thin wall is ONE D7 logical cell = 2 display cols = a solid
    495  f97f							;   PF bit-PAIR whose left and right neighbouring cells are empty. The
    496  f97f							;   emitted cells are pair-aligned (both bits of a cell are always written
    497  f97f							;   together: pf_values, ClearPFColumn, PhMaskTab), so ONE solidity read
    498  f97f							;   per cell covers both cols, and vertical extent needs no data: each row
    499  f97f							;   is tested on its own (the old rect h is exactly the run of thin rows —
    500  f97f							;   find_rectangles stops a w==1 rect at a row that joins a wider run, and
    501  f97f							;   so does the neighbour test). Col 0 (screen border, and its mirror col
    502  f97f							;   39) is never destroyable — the old `rect.x == 0` skip.
    503  f97f							;   Double-score guard = the buffer: the punched pair is empty, so a second
    504  f97f							;   blast in the same room finds no cell (the old WallMask bits and PairGone
    505  f97f							;   are gone; walls return on re-entry, D1-B). WallMask (BombPacked b3-6) is
    506  f97f							;   retired: HotOverlapBody now tests its parent hot cell's PF bit.
    507  f97f							;   Cost: ≤4 cells × 3 rows × ~3 cell probes; blast edge only.
    508  f97f
