    763  fe2b							; --- pin FIRST: the rider stays on the raft even on a TURN frame --------
    764  fe2b							; A raft boxed in by solid row-2 cells (or parked against a rail) turns
    765  fe2b							; every frame and never moves; the turn path returns before the carry, so
    766  fe2b							; pinning here is what keeps a rider standing on it. Without it he fell
    767  fe2b							; through a stuck raft into the water kill line and respawned forever
    768  fe2b							; (user report 2026-10-22: "player position keeps changing, zig-zags").
    769  fe2b							; The vyHi < 0 escape is the gate's `.RaftNoRide` (rising is not a ride).
    770  fe2b		       b5 e2		      lda	EnemyRamY,X
    771  fe2d		       38		      sec
    772  fe2e		       e9 16		      sbc	#RAFTER_PINFIT
